<title>GERMANY: Cologne Re 96 gp net profit rises 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Cologne Re 96 gp net profit rises 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurer Koelnische Rueckversicherung AG (Cologne Re) said on Monday its 1996 group net profit is expected to have risen around 25 percent to between 150 and 160 million marks.</p>
<p>The group said in a compulsory statement that its gross premium income in 1996 was up about 15 percent to 6.3 billion marks.</p>
<p>The group said that it had grown strongly in its life and health business.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
